{"files":[{"content":"#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10\n#define DT 0.01f\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f\n#define FORCE_TILE 3\n\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\n\nstatic void body_force_tail(Body *p, float dt, int n, int first) {\n  for (int i = first; i < n; ++i) {\n    const float xi = p[i].x;\n    const float yi = p[i].y;\n    const float zi = p[i].z;\n    float fx = 0.0f;\n    float fy = 0.0f;\n    float fz = 0.0f;\n\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n      const float dx = p[j].x - xi;\n      const float dy = p[j].y - yi;\n      const float dz = p[j].z - zi;\n      const float sqrd_dist = dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz + SOFTENING;\n      const float inv_dist = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n      const float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n\n      fx += dx * inv_dist3;\n      fy += dy * inv_dist3;\n      fz += dz * inv_dist3;\n    }\n\n    p[i].vx += dt * fx;\n    p[i].vy += dt * fy;\n    p[i].vz += dt * fz;\n  }\n}\n\nstatic void body_force_tiled(Body *p, float dt, int n) {\n  const int bulk_end = n - n % FORCE_TILE;\n\n#pragma omp for schedule(static)\n  for (int base = 0; base < bulk_end; base += FORCE_TILE) {\n    const int i0 = base;\n    const int i1 = base + 1;\n    const int i2 = base + 2;\n    const float xi0 = p[i0].x;\n    const float yi0 = p[i0].y;\n    const float zi0 = p[i0].z;\n    const float xi1 = p[i1].x;\n    const float yi1 = p[i1].y;\n    const float zi1 = p[i1].z;\n    const float xi2 = p[i2].x;\n    const float yi2 = p[i2].y;\n    const float zi2 = p[i2].z;\n    float fx0 = 0.0f;\n    float fy0 = 0.0f;\n    float fz0 = 0.0f;\n    float fx1 = 0.0f;\n    float fy1 = 0.0f;\n    float fz1 = 0.0f;\n    float fx2 = 0.0f;\n    float fy2 = 0.0f;\n    float fz2 = 0.0f;\n\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n      const float xj = p[j].x;\n      const float yj = p[j].y;\n      const float zj = p[j].z;\n\n      const float dx0 = xj - xi0;\n      const float dy0 = yj - yi0;\n      const float dz0 = zj - zi0;\n      const float sqrd_dist0 = dx0 * dx0 + dy0 * dy0 + dz0 * dz0 + SOFTENING;\n      const float inv_dist0 = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist0);\n      const float inv_dist30 = inv_dist0 * inv_dist0 * inv_dist0;\n      fx0 += dx0 * inv_dist30;\n      fy0 += dy0 * inv_dist30;\n      fz0 += dz0 * inv_dist30;\n\n      const float dx1 = xj - xi1;\n      const float dy1 = yj - yi1;\n      const float dz1 = zj - zi1;\n      const float sqrd_dist1 = dx1 * dx1 + dy1 * dy1 + dz1 * dz1 + SOFTENING;\n      const float inv_dist1 = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist1);\n      const float inv_dist31 = inv_dist1 * inv_dist1 * inv_dist1;\n      fx1 += dx1 * inv_dist31;\n      fy1 += dy1 * inv_dist31;\n      fz1 += dz1 * inv_dist31;\n\n      const float dx2 = xj - xi2;\n      const float dy2 = yj - yi2;\n      const float dz2 = zj - zi2;\n      const float sqrd_dist2 = dx2 * dx2 + dy2 * dy2 + dz2 * dz2 + SOFTENING;\n      const float inv_dist2 = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist2);\n      const float inv_dist32 = inv_dist2 * inv_dist2 * inv_dist2;\n      fx2 += dx2 * inv_dist32;\n      fy2 += dy2 * inv_dist32;\n      fz2 += dz2 * inv_dist32;\n    }\n\n    p[i0].vx += dt * fx0;\n    p[i0].vy += dt * fy0;\n    p[i0].vz += dt * fz0;\n    p[i1].vx += dt * fx1;\n    p[i1].vy += dt * fy1;\n    p[i1].vz += dt * fz1;\n    p[i2].vx += dt * fx2;\n    p[i2].vy += dt * fy2;\n    p[i2].vz += dt * fz2;\n  }\n\n  if (bulk_end != n) {\n#pragma omp single\n    {\n      body_force_tail(p, dt, n, bulk_end);\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n\n  return bodies;\n}\n\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n}\n\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\n  int nbodies;\n\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\n\n#pragma omp parallel\n  {\n    for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; ++iter) {\n      body_force_tiled(bodies, DT, nbodies);\n\n#pragma omp for schedule(static)\n      for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n        bodies[i].x += bodies[i].vx * DT;\n        bodies[i].y += bodies[i].vy * DT;\n        bodies[i].z += bodies[i].vz * DT;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\n\n  free(bodies);\n\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n}\n","path":"src/nbody.c"}],"hypothesis":"Processing three target bodies per force tile reuses each streamed source position while retaining each target body's ascending-j accumulation order; static tiled work sharing should improve locality and instruction-level parallelism on four ARM64 cores.","notes":"The force and integration phases remain separated by implicit OpenMP worksharing barriers, and binary I/O plus the original floating-point expressions are retained.","sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Tile the outer force loop in fixed groups of three targets, reusing each source position load across three independent scalar accumulators.","Keep one OpenMP team across all time steps and use static contiguous work sharing for tiled force work and position integration."]}